// Landscape Expansion Index, 30 m buffer, Liu et al. (2010).
// Shares are the percentage of NEW built-up cells in each class.
// sharesByPatch counts patches instead of cells - a handful of large
// infill patches can dominate the area share while most patches are
// small leapfrog specks, so both are reported.

